    "verdict": "`net` = tr_M^{z=1} - h*(coefficient of the longest element), exactly, ON H_3(q) -- it FAILS at n = 4 (11 of 24; see qbeta_rank_one_identity_is_n3_only_probe), so it is an n=3 fact and not a characterisation of the functionals; the conclusions below are unaffected because each is evaluated on Delta in H_3(q). Measured on all six basis elements. That sharpens the corpus's 'genuinely distinct functionals' to a single rank-one difference supported on w_0, and turns its companion 'they agree precisely when z=1' into a statement about Delta's SUPPORT -- Delta has zero w_0 coordinate -- rather than about the functionals, which differ by h on T_{w_0} at EVERY z. Consequences: the ladder phase is a transport WITHIN one family, 2*alpha(z) = tr_M^1(Delta) - tr_M^z(Delta); and since tr_M^{z=1} annihilates [H,H], the whole z-free floor is the rank-one term. Chasing that through gives the closed form the identity was missing: b_(2,1) = 0, so a_(2,1) IS the Markov weight y_(2,1)(1), and     net(dC) = -h * y_(2,1)(1)  -- exact, and stated entirely inside the Ocneanu family with no `net`-specific object left in it. Read with chi^(2,1)(Delta) = 0 from the block resolution: the 2-dimensional block contributes nothing to the trace-visible part of the phase and everything to the trace-invisible part. Its contribution was never absent -- it was in the sector no trace can see. Scope-(a): derives no correction, proposes no value, wires nothing."
